/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Prepare the platform services that are deliberately outside the Lamassu chart:"},"201":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a Kubernetes 1.24+ cluster and Helm 3.2+"},"202":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable PostgreSQL server and a role allowed to create databases and schemas"},"203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable RabbitMQ broker and credentials"},"204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"an OIDC provider, normally Keycloak, with a realm/tenant and client for Lamassu"},"205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Envoy Gateway 1.8+ and a `GatewayClass`"},"206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"cert-manager 1.14+; for trusted TLS, either a trusted issuer or a Kubernetes TLS Secret"},"207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a StorageClass and an external traffic design"},"208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart defaults to a `GatewayClass` named `eg`. Change `gateway.className` if your platform team uses another name."},"209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"You provide the PostgreSQL server. The chart's pre-install job connects with the supplied credentials, creates the required `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu. The current chart renders its self-signed issuer and CA certificate resources even when `tls.type: external` makes the Gateway use an existing TLS Secret. Selecting external TLS therefore does not remove the cert-manager prerequisite."},"214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If your values file still carries the legacy gateway JWT validation settings — `auth.oidc.apiGateway.jwks`, `auth.authorization.rolesClaim` or `auth.authorization.roles.admin` — remove them. The migration guide `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/3.8.0->4.0.0.md` documents their removal with no compatibility aliases, and `values.schema.json` rejects the leftover blocks instead of silently ignoring them. The replacements are `services.authz.jwkUrl` and `services.authz.bootstrap`, already shown in the example above."},"218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it:"},"219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"`amqp.tls: true` selects AMQPS in every event-bus configuration block. The default port stays `5672` and does not change automatically when TLS is enabled, so set `amqp.port` to the broker's TLS listener, commonly `5671`."},"220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"With no CA Secret configured, the event-bus clients use the system-trusted CAs. To trust a private CA, create a Secret in the release namespace containing the CA certificate in PEM format and set `amqp.ca.secretName` (and `amqp.ca.certificateKey` if the data key is not `ca.crt`)."},"221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"For brokers that require mutual TLS, create a Secret containing the client certificate and private key and set `amqp.client.secretName` (with `amqp.client.certificateKey` and `amqp.client.privateKeyKey` if the data keys are not `tls.crt` and `tls.key`)."},"222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"The chart mounts configured Secrets read-only into every AMQP-consuming workload: the CA certificate under `/etc/lamassu/amqp/ca` and the client certificate and key under `/etc/lamassu/amqp/client`. The mounted file names are always `ca.crt`, `tls.crt` and `tls.key` — the `certificateKey` and `privateKeyKey` values rename only the Secret data keys, never the on-disk paths. The client private key is mounted with restrictive permissions (`defaultMode: 0440`; the CA volume uses `0444`), which works because the chart adds `fsGroup` to the pod security context when `amqp.client.secretName` is set — it uses the container `runAsGroup` (default `65532`) when `fsGroup` is not already set."},"223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"Both Secret options require `amqp.tls: true`: `values.schema.json` rejects a non-empty `secretName` when `tls` is false, rejects unknown keys and rejects data-key names outside `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$`. The referenced Secret must exist in the release namespace or the consuming pods fail to start."},"224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"The AMQP client loads certificates at startup, so restart the consuming pods after updating either Secret. Changing any `amqp` value rolls the consuming pods through the `checksum/config` annotation, but a change to Secret content alone does not trigger a rollout."},"225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#amqp-tls-amqps","content":"Per the migration guide `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/3.8.0->4.0.0.md`: in 3.8.0 `amqp.tls` was not applied and event-bus clients used plaintext AMQP; from 4.0.0, `amqp.tls: true` switches them to AMQPS. Set `amqp.port` to the broker TLS listener before upgrading, or set `amqp.tls: false` to keep plaintext AMQP."},"226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA storage before increasing VA replicas"},"237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"managed OIDC roles and removal of evaluation credentials"},"238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a trusted TLS issuer or externally managed certificate"},"239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-42/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":